Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-01-2000||12:02 PM||||not one thats measureable on a dyno.. you will notice the cars idle change, and it'll warm up different. if you change the intake, and exhaust you'll notice a difference with a chip cause it changes the fuel curve and ign. timing to utilize the mods but on a stock car don't waste your money.. buy an MSD 6a or a Crane HI6s. you'll notice a larger improvement... or if you have an automatic it'll change the shift points. but not enough to matter. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||count_iblis||11-01-2000||12:16 PM||||MSD 6a? <P>------------------<BR>COUNTIBLIS <BR>"HUG YOUR KIDS SPANK THE SOUND BARRIER"||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||11-01-2000||04:24 PM||||yeah all the benefits of 6AL the milti-spark 20* and capacitave discharge after 3400rpm but no revlimiter and you'll save $50. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||11-01-2000||07:42 PM||||I robbed the MSD 6a and blaster 2 coil off my Suburban for the Fiero- Seemed to smooth out the idle a little and helped out a flat spot that happened just above idle. I think it was a worthwhile add on-especially since I already had it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-01-2000||10:43 PM||||Stupid question but where can you get them. I hate buying things at the dealership here, but is that the only place I will find them? I too have a hypertech chip and noticed very little difference. I cant tell for sure if that smoothed out the idle or the new coil did, but I wouldnt pay the money for it again for a stock engine. It might come in useful for the new engine though.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleeper||11-02-2000||01:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>on a stock car don't waste your money<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know about hypertech but I have a J.E.T. chip and it has boosted up the powerband in my fiero with a stock motor, gas goes quicker but what the hay.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||11-02-2000||09:04 AM||||I used the ADS, and the Hypertechs ones and saw MAYBE 4hp on the dyno... the MSD can be purchased at <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A>   and many local speed shops... about $120 and the Accel Super coil at the same places... for about $40... <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
